# Case File Auditor: "... whenever you solve a Case, look at the top six cards of your library." (CR 719.3b, 603.2). Bot1's Auditor enters on turn 1 and takes a Case of the Gateway Express from
# the top six. On turn 2 Bot2 casts and, at its end step, solves its own Case of the Crimson Pulse (no cards in hand): Bot1's Auditor does not look at anything, so Bot1's library and hand are as they were.
# On turn 3 Bot1 attacks with three Memnite, casts the Gateway Express in its second main phase, and it is solved at Bot1's end step; the Auditor looks at the top six, a Pacifism and five Plains,
